1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19701, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01EC3pYeHd25z5jN2CwYHpr2", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19701, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_012gKemUyGvduApuFJQs33uD", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20001, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_012gKemUyGvduApuFJQs33uD", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20001, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012gKemUyGvduApuFJQs33uD", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 24404, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01BZvRwdeFWmDU2Hd4kMTY6Q", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollout. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and look into the rollout orchestrator error.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55004, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01BZvRwdeFWmDU2Hd4kMTY6Q", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55004, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01BZvRwdeFWmDU2Hd4kMTY6Q", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 56692, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0135VD6HJkUXZqunRURzSyd8", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56992, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0135VD6HJkUXZqunRURzSyd8", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56992, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0135VD6HJkUXZqunRURzSyd8", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 61649, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 (the latest deploy) was unhealthy in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%.\n- I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.0 was healthy before, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the regions on different versions. I checked the state and ran the same rollback again, and it finished.\n- All three regions are now on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- I asked for a SEV2 for checkout-api describing the bad release, the rollback and the stalled rollout, and noted that v2.3.1 was also unhealthy in staging.\n- The request timed out. Instead of resending it, I checked the incident list: INC-0001 had been created, so only one person was paged.\n- The incident lists two follow-ups: finding why v2.3.1 failed, and looking into the orchestrator error.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011YEmPKqVrJGb9PjRx3taqa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PR9PSkWYt32ZWdi3vVdC2c", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_019SatogmttL8fDfaPkcd3mA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01YAXKQprubrNbsgGMvktrQG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway through. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I'll retry it once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Y9EWUAtBSrnYktP6gXY7FK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01EC3pYeHd25z5jN2CwYHpr2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012gKemUyGvduApuFJQs33uD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BZvRwdeFWmDU2Hd4kMTY6Q", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. Its release candidate v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, leaving regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollout. All three regions now run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and look into the rollout orchestrator error.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_0135VD6HJkUXZqunRURzSyd8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 (the latest deploy) was unhealthy in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%.\n- I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.0 was healthy before, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the regions on different versions. I checked the state and ran the same rollback again, and it finished.\n- All three regions are now on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- I asked for a SEV2 for checkout-api describing the bad release, the rollback and the stalled rollout, and noted that v2.3.1 was also unhealthy in staging.\n- The request timed out. Instead of resending it, I checked the incident list: INC-0001 had been created, so only one person was paged.\n- The incident lists two follow-ups: finding why v2.3.1 failed, and looking into the orchestrator error.", "type": "text"}]}]}